@startuml websocket-serving-flow

title WebSocket Serving — Upgrade, Subscribe, Live Feed, and Hydration (CP6)

participant Browser
participant "API\n(WS Server)" as API
database "Redis\n(redisSub — subscriber only)" as Redis
database "Redis\n(redis — commands only)" as RedisLive
database "TimescaleDB\n(alerts)" as DB

note over API, Redis
  Two separate Redis connections required.
  redisSub: SUBSCRIBE only — cannot issue commands.
  redis: HGETALL, SCAN, etc — cannot SUBSCRIBE.
end note

== WebSocket upgrade ==

Browser -> API : HTTP Upgrade\nCookie: sentinel_jwt=...
API -> API : verify JWT from cookie\nextract user_id
alt token invalid or missing
  API --> Browser : 401 Unauthorized\n(upgrade rejected)
else token valid
  API --> Browser : 101 Switching Protocols
end

== Client declares viewport ==

Browser -> API : { type: "subscribe",\n  bbox: [minLat, minLon, maxLat, maxLon] }
API -> API : store bbox for this connection

== Redis subscriber setup (on API startup) ==

API -> Redis : SUBSCRIBE position-updates alert-events
note right of API
  Dedicated subscriber connection.
  Cannot issue regular Redis commands
  on a subscribed connection.
end note

== Live position update ==

Redis -> API : PUBLISH position-updates\n{ entity_id, lat, lon, timestamp_ms, ... }
API -> API : parse lat, lon\ncheck against each connection's bbox
alt entity within client bbox
  API --> Browser : WS frame\n{ entity_id, lat, lon, timestamp_ms, ... }
else entity outside bbox
  API -> API : skip — do not forward
end

== Live alert event ==

Redis -> API : PUBLISH alert-events\n{ alert_id, alert_type, status, ... }
note right of API
  Alert events go to all connected clients.
  No bbox filter — alerts are global.
end note
API --> Browser : WS frame\n{ alert_id, alert_type, status, ... }

== Dashboard hydration — GET /entities/live ==

Browser -> API : GET /entities/live?bbox=minLat,minLon,maxLat,maxLon\nCookie: sentinel_jwt=...
API -> API : requireAuth: verify JWT
API -> RedisLive : SCAN entity:live:*\nHGETALL each hash
API -> API : filter by bbox\nfilter stale (last_seen_ms < now - 2x threshold)\ncap at 500\nparse floats, empty string → null
API --> Browser : 200 [ entity snapshots ]

== Reconnect recovery ==

note over Browser, DB
  On WebSocket disconnect, client re-runs full hydration:
  1. GET /entities/live  — re-seeds map from Redis live state
  2. GET /alerts         — re-seeds alert panel from TimescaleDB
  3. Open new WebSocket  — send subscribe with current bbox
  Messages missed during the gap are recovered from
  Redis and TimescaleDB, not from pub/sub replay.
end note

@enduml
